WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.616 --> 00:00:07.970
SPEAKER 1: May you serve the
Institute with all the skill,

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.575
wisdom, dedication--

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:13.540
SPEAKER 2: He is tremendously
prepared for this job.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.140
He knows MIT inside and out.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.390
He is a community builder.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:27.580
SPEAKER 3: He empowers and
energizes and gets so much of

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.500
the community trying
new things.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.760
SPEAKER 4: I think it's awesome
that he was already

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.800
championing MITx when
he was the provost.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.050
And so, I think as we go forward
Edx will get a lot of

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.550
attention and I'm really
excited about that.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:51.680
DR. L. RAFAEL REIF: The MIT
I know loves challenges.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:56.570
The MIT I know solves the
unsolvable, shapes the future,

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:59.730
and serves our nation
and the world.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:04.480
The MIT I know and love does
not stand on the sidelines.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:10.335
SPEAKER 5: One community--

00:01:10.335 --> 00:01:11.160
SPEAKER 6: --together--

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:11.970
SPEAKER 7: --in service.

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.340
SPEAKER 8: [INAUDIBLE] back
into a user interface.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.570
This is actually
our prototype.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.540
SPEAKER 3: A big part of
this week's events

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:18.960
are these three symposia.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.030
And I think they're a critical
part because they do showcase

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:24.780
elements of MIT, but they
also have begun

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.775
dialogue as we look forward.

00:01:26.775 --> 00:01:29.720
SPEAKER 9: I'll spend some time
talking about how online

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:33.040
learning is borrowing from
gaming technologies.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:36.810
SPEAKER 10: There's this giant
quilt that is MIT.

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:39.960
And there are so many different
beautiful patches there that

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.300
are being built, even as we
speak, and some have been

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.440
around for a long time.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.790
SPEAKER 11: MIT has, and still
does, shape amazing

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:48.780
individuals that see the
entire world as their

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:50.030
playground.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:57.154
SPEAKER 1: Ladies and gentlemen,
the 17th President

00:01:57.154 --> 00:01:59.509
of the Massachusetts Institute
of Technology,

00:01:59.509 --> 00:02:02.806
Dr. L. Rafael Reif.

00:02:02.806 --> 00:02:06.280
SPEAKER 12: Rafael Reif is well
known to us at Harvard

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:09.650
for his insight and
his judgment.

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:15.430
He is a generous and genuine
convener who listens as much

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:18.170
as he speaks.

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:22.140
SPEAKER 13: We like the rhythm
of his name, Rafael Reif.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.859
Thus, you are about to hear
a rumba for Rafael Reif.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:34.600
DR. L. RAFAEL REIF: Society
continues to need what the

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:35.150
residential

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:39.250
research university does
better than any other

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.730
institution--

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:44.820
incubate brilliant, young talent
and create the new

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:47.860
knowledge and innovation
that fuel our society.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:57.390
I will lead MIT to continue to
make significant contributions

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:59.140
in the area of race and

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:02.050
diversity, equity, and inclusion.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:04.350
We have many compelling
suggestions

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.840
for practical change.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:10.410
These include better ways to
search for and mentor new

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:13.910
talent and to improve the
orientation process for new

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:16.390
members of our community.

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:18.370
SPEAKER 14: We're able to reach
out to a lot of people,

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:19.940
have a run on campus.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.050
We're promoting a lot of ideals
here, obviously, like

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:24.060
health and fitness, Habitat
for Humanity, general

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:26.580
community wellness, and, like,
community joining together,

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.720
and, of course, like celebrate
our new president.

00:03:45.187 --> 00:03:48.480
SPEAKER 15: Around the Dome
Campus Quest is a campus-wide

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:49.700
scavenger hunt.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:51.880
SPEAKER 16: All the groups just
go through and see how

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.770
many of the challenges
they can complete.

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:56.690
SPEAKER 15: Things like the LED
Light-Up Challenge, the

00:03:56.690 --> 00:04:01.410
Origami Challenge, and then
we had a Bungee Run.

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:03.150
SPEAKER 16: It's a really great
reminder that we have

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:05.240
such a strong community here and
that the culture is really

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:06.490
important to everyone.

00:04:09.288 --> 00:04:13.890
SPEAKER 12: And now, despite
silently suffering torment and

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:18.149
humiliation these many years
as the victim of MIT's

00:04:18.149 --> 00:04:23.000
creative hackers, John Harvard
has dressed himself up for

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.790
today's occasion.

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:27.730
President Reif, on behalf of
the Red Brick School up the

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:31.970
street, I present a symbol of
our lasting friendship.

00:04:34.905 --> 00:04:53.220
[APPLAUSE]

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.290
SPEAKER 17: We had an
inauguration reception

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:58.140
luncheon for our 17th
President, Dr.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:04:59.730
Rafael Reif, today.

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:00.535
DR. L. RAFAEL REIF: Thank you.

00:05:00.535 --> 00:05:01.310
Good meeting you.

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:02.290
Thank you very much.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:04.950
SPEAKER 17: And it was for all
of the support staff here.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:07.210
He wanted to meet all of
the support staff.

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:08.285
DR. L. RAFAEL REIF: It was
very nice meeting you.

00:05:08.285 --> 00:05:10.980
SPEAKER 18: It's such a pleasure
to be recognized and

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:12.090
to see President.

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:15.010
It was very nice that he could
make it and took his time and

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:17.960
came and said thank you to us.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:19.210
That was very special.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.840
DR. L. RAFAEL REIF:
We are all in this

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:34.640
great enterprise together.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:37.460
We have a great deal
to accomplish, and

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:39.120
the world is waiting.

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:40.960
So let's get started.

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:59.426
[APPLAUSE]

